Classic script, no modules, no library. At load it defines globalThis.PastaTimeline and, when `module` exists, sets module.exports = PastaTimeline, so node can require() it; it touches no DOM at load. All times are epoch milliseconds.

PastaTimeline = {
  statusClass(status: string, typeInfo: {initial: string, finish: string[]} | undefined):
      "idle" | "active" | "review" | "done" | "warn",      // the ordered rules in the strategy's Part 3
  fold(data: ReplayJson): Model,
      // Model.pages: PageRec[], Model.byId: Map<string, PageRec>, Model.t0, Model.t1,
      // Model.recordingStart: number | null  (ts of the present events; null when the log has none)
      // present for an unknown page: born = its ts; present for a known page: silent resync at its ts;
      // a known page no present event names: endedAt = recordingStart
  isShown(m: Model, p: PageRec, T: number): boolean,
      // born <= T, not ended or deleted at or before T, and neither p nor any ancestor (by the parent each had at T)
      // archived at T; a parent id not in m.byId ends the walk
  statusAt(p: PageRec, T: number): string | null,   // null before born
  titleAt(p: PageRec, T: number): string | null,
  parentAt(p: PageRec, T: number): string | null,
  layoutMetro(m: Model): { height: number },        // assigns each PageRec a track (or none when hidden for good from its first moment) and y in px
  playheadStep(T: number, dtSeconds: number, speedDaysPerSecond: number, nextEventTs: number | null): number,
      // T + dtSeconds * speedDaysPerSecond * 86_400_000, multiplied by 6 when nextEventTs - T > 21_600_000; no clamping
  mount(root: HTMLElement): void           // reads root.dataset.src, fetches it, folds, lays out, wires the controls, starts playing at t0
}
PageRec carries at least: id, type, born, present (bool: first seen in the baseline), finishT (number | null: ts of its first move into a finish status), endedAt (number | null), track (number | null). Its other fields are the builder's.
The script ignores unknown event kinds, events for pages it has not seen, and unknown top-level keys.

